<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  Where Calc stops formatting a wrapping cell's lines, and why the ones it stops at are not in
  its PDF's text layer at all.

  THIS IS NOT A CLIP.  `ScOutputData::DrawEditStandard` calls
  `EnableSkipOutsideFormat(meVerJust==Top || meVerJust==Standard)` (output2.cxx:3115) and the
  EditEngine then refuses to *format* the lines past the paper height
  (`ImpEditEngine::CreateLines`, impedit3.cxx:1801-1806), with a coarser guard one level up
  (impedit3.cxx:676-680) that drops a whole paragraph whose first line would start past it.
  So those lines are never laid out, never drawn, and never reach the text layer — which is
  what makes this the one rule on the cell-text path that a word count can see.

  The paper height is the cell's own, `rAlignRect.GetHeight() - nTopM - nBottomM`
  (`calcPaperSize`, output2.cxx:2684-2700), and `calcPaperSize` is called only under
  `if (rParam.mbBreak)`: a cell that does not wrap keeps the initial Size(1000000, 1000000)
  and is never truncated however many hard breaks it holds.

  One 4 cm column on A4 with 2 cm margins, Liberation Sans 10 pt, whose pitch here is 11.20 pt.
  ODF's default cell margin is 0.035 cm a side, so the paper height is the row height less
  1.98 pt.  Every figure below is read off LibreOffice 26.2.4.2's own output for this file.

  row 1  a  1 cm, wrap, valign TOP.      paper 26.37 pt = 2.35 pitches.  4 lines, a001..a016.
                                          The minimum: "Format at least two lines though"
                                          (impedit3.cxx:1799) is four counted from outside.
  row 2  b  58 pt, wrap, valign TOP.      paper 56.02 pt = 5.002 pitches.  6 lines, b001..b024.
                                          The comparison is strict, so an exact multiple gets
                                          one line more than the multiple — ceil would say 5.
  row 3  c  3 cm, wrap, valign TOP.       paper 83.06 pt = 7.42 pitches.  8 lines, c001..c032.
  row 4  d  1 cm, wrap, valign BOTTOM.    NOT truncated: 15 lines, all 60 tokens.  The guard
                                          names Top and Standard and nothing else.
  row 5  e  1 cm, wrap, valign MIDDLE.    NOT truncated: 15 lines, all 60 tokens.
  row 6  f  1 cm, NO WRAP, twenty hard-break paragraphs.  All 20 drawn: no wrap, no paper.
  row 7  g  1 cm, wrap, TOP, six one-line paragraphs.  3 drawn — the paragraph guard, which
                                          gives no paragraph after the first the four-line
                                          allowance.
  row 8  h  1 cm, wrap, valign UNSTATED (Standard).  Truncated to 4 lines, h001..h016, and
                                          still placed from the bottom of the row.
  row 9  i  3 cm, wrap, TOP, three tokens.  The control: one line, nothing dropped.
-->
<office:document xmlns:office="urn:oasis:names:tc:opendocument:xmlns:office:1.0"
 xmlns:style="urn:oasis:names:tc:opendocument:xmlns:style:1.0"
 xmlns:text="urn:oasis:names:tc:opendocument:xmlns:text:1.0"
 xmlns:table="urn:oasis:names:tc:opendocument:xmlns:table:1.0"
